Error [E2805]: Invalid HTTP route `/users/{id}`: brace interpolation is not allowed in route patterns; it is indistinguishable from the retired `{name}` parameter spelling
  --> http_route_invalid_literal.jet:9:16
    |
  9 |     router.get("/users/{id}", handle)
    |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Route patterns use one canonical grammar; ambiguous escapes, traversal, duplicate names, and retired markers would make routing and audit metadata disagree
 Fix: Use `:name` for one segment or final `*name` for a catch-all; percent-encode a literal leading `:` or `*`, and never encode `/`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2805

Error [E2805]: Invalid HTTP route `/teams/{name}`: use `:name` or final `*name`; braces are not route markers
  --> http_route_invalid_literal.jet:11:16
    |
 11 |     router.get(doubled, handle)
    |                ^^^^^^^
 Why: Route patterns use one canonical grammar; ambiguous escapes, traversal, duplicate names, and retired markers would make routing and audit metadata disagree
 Fix: Use `:name` for one segment or final `*name` for a catch-all; percent-encode a literal leading `:` or `*`, and never encode `/`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2805

Error [E0302]: `.scheme` only works on struct and tuple values
  --> Core/http/http.jet:886:15
    |
886 |     if parsed.scheme != "http" && parsed.scheme != "https" -> return false
    |               ^^^^^^
 Why: Enums and other values use methods or pattern tests instead
 Fix: Use a struct or tuple value before `.scheme`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0302

